Undefined scenarios:
  1) Todos persist after page reload # features/persistence.feature:11
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I create a todo "Buy milk"
       And I create a todo "Walk dog"
       And I mark "Walk dog" as completed
       When I reload the page
       Then I see 2 todos in the list
       And "Walk dog" has class "completed"
       And "Buy milk" does not have class "completed"
  2) localStorage uses correct key and format # features/persistence.feature:20
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
       Then localStorage contains a key matching "todos-"
       And the stored value is valid JSON with objects having keys "id", "title", "completed"
  3) Editing state is not persisted # features/persistence.feature:27
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
       And I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
       When I reload the page
       Then "Buy milk" does not have class "editing"
  4) localStorage clears when all todos are deleted # features/persistence.feature:35
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
       When I delete "Buy milk"
       Then the localStorage key is empty or absent
  5) All route shows every todo # features/routing.feature:12
       Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
       And "Walk dog" is marked completed
       Given I navigate to "#/"
       Then I see 2 todos in the list
       And the "All" filter link has class "selected"
  6) Active route shows only incomplete todos # features/routing.feature:19
       Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
       And "Walk dog" is marked completed
       Given I navigate to "#/active"
       Then I see 1 todo in the list
       And I see a todo with title "Buy milk"
       And I do not see a todo with title "Walk dog"
       And the "Active" filter link has class "selected"
  7) Completed route shows only done todos # features/routing.feature:28
       Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
       And "Walk dog" is marked completed
       Given I navigate to "#/completed"
       Then I see 1 todo in the list
       And I see a todo with title "Walk dog"
       And I do not see a todo with title "Buy milk"
       And the "Completed" filter link has class "selected"
  8) Completing a todo while on active filter hides it # features/routing.feature:37
       Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
       And "Walk dog" is marked completed
       Given I navigate to "#/active"
       When I mark "Buy milk" as completed
       Then I see 0 todos in the list
  9) Un-completing a todo while on completed filter hides it # features/routing.feature:42
       Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
       And "Walk dog" is marked completed
       Given I navigate to "#/completed"
       When I click the toggle checkbox for "Walk dog"
       Then I see 0 todos in the list
  10) Active filter persists on page reload # features/routing.feature:49
       Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
       And "Walk dog" is marked completed
       Given I navigate to "#/active"
       When I reload the page
       Then I see 1 todo in the list
       And the "Active" filter link has class "selected"
  11) Clear completed removes done todos from completed view # features/routing.feature:57
       Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
       And "Walk dog" is marked completed
       Given I navigate to "#/completed"
       When I click the clear-completed button
       Then I see 0 todos in the list
       And the clear-completed button is hidden
  12) Create a todo # features/todo-core.feature:11
       Given the app is loaded
       Given no todos exist
       When I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and press Enter
       Then I see 1 todo in the list with title "Buy milk"
       And the new-todo input is cleared
       And #main and #footer are visible
  13) Trim whitespace from new todo # features/todo-core.feature:18
       Given the app is loaded
       Given no todos exist
       When I type "   Walk dog   " into the new-todo input and press Enter
       Then I see 1 todo in the list with title "Walk dog"
  14) Ignore empty todo # features/todo-core.feature:23
       Given the app is loaded
       Given no todos exist
       When I type "" into the new-todo input and press Enter
       Then I see 0 todos in the list
  15) Ignore whitespace-only todo # features/todo-core.feature:28
       Given the app is loaded
       Given no todos exist
       When I type "   " into the new-todo input and press Enter
       Then I see 0 todos in the list
  16) Hide main and footer when no todos # features/todo-core.feature:35
       Given the app is loaded
       Given no todos exist
       Then #main is hidden
       And #footer is hidden
  17) Toggle a single todo # features/todo-core.feature:42
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
       When I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
       Then the todo "Buy milk" has class "completed"
       And its toggle checkbox is checked
  18) Mark all as complete # features/todo-core.feature:48
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
       When I click the toggle-all checkbox
       Then all todos have class "completed"
  19) Toggle-all reflects individual state # features/todo-core.feature:53
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
       And I mark "Walk dog" as completed
       When I inspect the toggle-all checkbox
       Then the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
  20) Toggle-all checks when all are complete # features/todo-core.feature:59
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
       And I mark "Buy milk" as completed
       And I mark "Walk dog" as completed
       When I inspect the toggle-all checkbox
       Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
  21) Delete a todo via destroy button # features/todo-core.feature:68
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
       When I click the destroy button for "Buy milk"
       Then I see 0 todos in the list
       And #main and #footer are hidden
  22) Display active count with singular # features/todo-core.feature:76
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
       Then the todo-count shows "1 item left"
  23) Display active count with plural # features/todo-core.feature:80
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
       And I mark "Walk dog" as completed
       Then the todo-count shows "1 item left"
  24) Display zero active count # features/todo-core.feature:85
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
       When I mark "Buy milk" as completed
       Then the todo-count shows "0 items left"
  25) Clear completed removes done todos # features/todo-core.feature:92
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
       And I mark "Buy milk" as completed
       When I click the clear-completed button
       Then I see 1 todo in the list
       And the clear-completed button is hidden
  26) Hide clear-completed when none completed # features/todo-core.feature:99
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
       Then the clear-completed button is hidden
  27) Clear completed toggles toggle-all unchecked # features/todo-core.feature:103
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
       And I mark "Buy milk" as completed
       And I mark "Walk dog" as completed
       And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
       When I click the clear-completed button
       Then the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
  28) Double-click activates editing mode # features/todo-core.feature:113
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
       When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
       Then the todo "Buy milk" has class "editing"
       And the edit input for "Buy milk" contains "Buy milk"
  29) Save edit on Enter # features/todo-core.feature:119
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
       And I am editing "Buy milk"
       When I type "Buy organic milk" into the edit input and press Enter
       Then I see a todo with title "Buy organic milk"
       And the todo "Buy organic milk" does not have class "editing"
  30) Save edit on blur # features/todo-core.feature:126
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
       And I am editing "Buy milk"
       When I type "Buy oat milk" into the edit input and blur
       Then I see a todo with title "Buy oat milk"
       And the todo "Buy oat milk" does not have class "editing"
  31) Trim edit input # features/todo-core.feature:133
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
       And I am editing "Buy milk"
       When I type "   Buy oat milk   " into the edit input and press Enter
       Then I see a todo with title "Buy oat milk"
  32) Destroy todo when edit is empty # features/todo-core.feature:139
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
       And I am editing "Buy milk"
       When I type "" into the edit input and press Enter
       Then I see 0 todos in the list
  33) Destroy todo when edit is whitespace # features/todo-core.feature:145
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
       And I am editing "Buy milk"
       When I type "   " into the edit input and press Enter
       Then I see 0 todos in the list
  34) Cancel edit with Escape # features/todo-core.feature:151
       Given the app is loaded
       Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
       And I am editing "Buy milk"
       When I press Escape while editing
       Then the todo "Buy milk" does not have class "editing"
       And I see a todo with title "Buy milk"
  35) new-todo input is autofocused on load # features/todo-core.feature:158
       Given the app is loaded
       Given the page is loaded
       Then the new-todo input has focus

